{"id": "EUVD-2026-103676", "enisaUuid": "ff6d96b2-5830-3030-b99a-316bd0bb54ba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: qcom: iris: fix runtime PM reference leaks\n\nUse pm_runtime_resume_and_get() in iris_enable_power_domains()\nto avoid leaking a runtime PM usage count on failure.\n\nAlso ensure pm_runtime_put_sync() is always called in\niris_disable_power_domains(), even when iris_opp_set_rate()\nfails, so runtime PM references remain balanced.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T14:45:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fff1ae8d0c8c97668e4cbcc6e1fd2cc740013795", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a52e76b63095e05d92f15f16f45421cab9789e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f87d7eda07fca21efe4b96169ae59007db46e60e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98437", "GHSA-2w8w-fc6j-3f4v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09427bd5-c1bb-34c4-b943-efa6b4d2f801", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <fff1ae8d0c8c97668e4cbcc6e1fd2cc740013795"}, {"id": "14935da8-a9d6-3c95-9b02-b1116bead9d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <f87d7eda07fca21efe4b96169ae59007db46e60e"}, {"id": "37dbbffb-e5db-3015-a69c-f1880e73e142", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "693aa1c3-2710-3f0e-a04d-6862b8a93258", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a4d6ffa6-5a26-3040-a17f-e49710b0314f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "da2c7645-40a9-3e84-baa5-d4397a12569d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb8a95aa038e099f5ec82c466e996b006e05abd7 <7a52e76b63095e05d92f15f16f45421cab97